{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Strengthen laws to identify and remove malicious online content and bots",
        "additional_details": "We believe the impact of the destruction of Russian data centres highlights the potential scale of coordinated online manipulation.\r\n\r\nWe call on the Government to introduce stronger legislation requiring social media companies to actively detect, investigate and disrupt coordinated bot networks, organised trolling and deliberate disinformation campaigns. Platforms must be held accountable for allowing manipulation that fuels hatred, undermines public trust and threatens democratic processes. Independent oversight, transparent reporting and meaningful penalties are essential to protecting the public and safeguarding democracy.\r\n",
        "background": "The Government must strengthen legal responsibilities for social media platforms to identify and remove malicious bots, organised trolling and deliberate disinformation.",
